A||||3||4Banger Bandit||Need some advice guys...
Z||000000||4Banger Bandit||09-01-99||04:49 PM||||Here's what I'm doing... I'm transfering the headlight assemblies from my '85 2M4 to my '87 GT(which doesn't have any headlights or brackets at all) and I have some questions...  The brackets are the same, and they swapped-out just fine, but there is an extra blue wire on the headlight motor on the '85. This is in addition to the grey and green wire which seem to be the same. Anybody know what this blue wire is for??? I couldn't find it in the wiring diagram.  I still have the motors for the '87, but they dont' seem to work very well.  The ones on the '85 work great though.  I'd like to use them.  Anybody know anything about this??<br>thanks..
Z||000001||PaUL||09-01-99||05:39 PM||||The 87 and later models came with a different headlight actuator motor. The newer ones have an external electronic control module with just 2 wires goint to the motors. The older onew have 3 wires coming from a relay. Youd need to swap in the older relay to make it all work.
Z||000002||Greg Piet||09-01-99||06:12 PM||||There are instructions as how to convert over  to teh new style motors at the following address<br>www.tir.com/~jaski/headlight.htm
Z||000003||theogre||09-01-99||07:03 PM||||he doesn't need to convert,,, he just needs the 2 new motors.... He already has the controls for them. The new motors should just drop into the frames as far as I know.
